{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-symmetric-point-channel-collapse","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:symmetric-point-channel-collapse","kind":"remark","title":"Channel collapse across all three operator assignments","interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-symmetric-point-channel-collapse","tags":["symmetric-point","hecke","degeneration"],"text":"symmetric-point-channel-collapse-remark.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:symmetric-point-channel-collapse\"></a><p>Any family of operator assignments drawn from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{\\sigma,\\ \\sigma^{-1},\\ (\\sigma + \\sigma^{-1})/2\\}</code> collapses to a single operator under the specialisation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code> of the Hecke relation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma - q)(\\sigma + q^{-1}) = 0</code>, which at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code> reads <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma^2 = 1</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/symmetric-point-channel-collapse-remark.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.4.2"}
